   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend a chapter of the laws of 2016, amending the general municipal law, the public authorities law, and the tax law, relating to certain recording taxes, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S979",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S979-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6, Chap of 2016 (as proposed in S.7442 & A.9490)",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S979\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2016, amending the general\nmunicipal law, the public authorities law, and the tax law, relating\nto certain recording taxes, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo change the effective date of Chapter 394 of the Laws of 2016.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would change the effective date of Chapter 394 of the Laws\nof 2016 from immediately to July 1, 2016.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe immediate effective date of Chapter 394 of the Laws of 2016 may\ninterfere with the completion of several pending projects and\nnecessitate changes to contractual arrangements made by certain\nindustrial development agencies. Changing the effective date to a\npoint in the future will enable those agencies to ensure that future\nproject agreements comply with the new restriction on exempting the\nportion of mortgage recording taxes that go to transportation\ndistricts.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have\nbeen in full force and effect on and after a chapter of the laws of\n2016, amending the General Municipal Law, the Public Authorities Law,\nand the Tax Law, relating to certain recording taxes, as proposed in\nlegislative bill numbers A.9490 and S.7442, takes effect.\n",
